%N A289555 Numbers that are not the product of two distinct composite numbers (A002808).
%C A289555 Numbers that are either the 4th power of a prime or have at most 3 prime factors (counted by multiplicity). - _Robert Israel_, Aug 02 2026
%H A289555 Robert Israel, <a href="/A289555/b289555.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%e A289555 Number 24 is not in the sequence because 24 = 4 * 6.
%p A289555 filter:= proc(n) local F;
%p A289555   F:= ifactors(n)[2][..,2];
%p A289555   convert(F,`+`) < 4 or F = [4]
%p A289555 end proc;
%p A289555 select(filter, [$1..100]); # _Robert Israel_, Aug 02 2026
%o A289555 (Magma) [n: n in [1..1000] | (#PrimeDivisors(n) eq 1 and NumberOfDivisors(n) lt 6) or (#PrimeDivisors(n) eq 2 and NumberOfDivisors(n) lt 8) or (#PrimeDivisors(n) ge 3 and NumberOfDivisors(n) lt 12) ];
%Y A289555 Complement of A289554.
%Y A289555 Cf. A246716 (with two distinct primes), A008578 (with two distinct nonprimes), A289553 (with two distinct noncomposites).
%K A289555 nonn,changed
%O A289555 1,2
%A A289555 _Jaroslav Krizek_, Jul 07 2017
